=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The helpdesk ticket #8155 does not reflect a real fault. A thorough multi-layer investigation of router16 and the entire Campus 1 path found no anomaly at any level.

**Control plane:** Router16 is up and running FRR OSPF normally. Its bond0 interface (10.2.2.1/24, bonding eth0+eth1 toward mswitch0) is in OSPF DR state with a Full adjacency to mswitch0 (router-ID 172.16.30.254). Its eth2 (172.30.1.1/24, toward router7) is in OSPF BDR state with a Full adjacency to router7 (192.168.10.1). Both adjacency timers are healthy; Dead Time is in the 33–35 s range out of a 40 s window — completely normal.

**Route propagation:** All three Campus 1 prefixes (172.16.10.0/24, 172.16.20.0/24, 172.16.30.0/24) are originated by mswitch0, learned by router16 (cost 10 via bond0), and then re-advertised into the rest of the OSPF domain. Router7 carries all three prefixes via 172.30.1.1 (router16), cost 20. No route is missing.

**Data plane:** End-hosts on all three campus VLANs (pc5 on VLAN 10, pc9 on VLAN 20, pc8 on VLAN 10, pc12 on VLAN 30) successfully ping remote routers (router10, router11, router1) with 0 % packet loss and sub-3 ms RTTs.

**Root cause:** There is no fault. The ticket was either raised in error, based on stale/transient monitoring data, or reflects a now-resolved event. No corrective action is required.
=== END ===